  "fashion": {
    "Early Emo (1980s–1990s)": "Weezer's Rivers Cuomo in 1994. The 'Buddy Holly' glasses and casual ringer tee represent the clean-cut and indie-influenced style that preceded the 2000s fashion boom. The fashion style of the Emo subculture has changed drastically over time. The popular image of the \"Emo Kid\" (black hair, eyeliner, and skinny jeans) is specific to the mid-2000s and bears little resemblance to the fashion of the original 1980s and 1990s scenes.",
    "Mainstream Emo (2000s)": "Gerard Way (2005) during the Three Cheers for Sweet Revenge era. His theatrical and vampire-inspired aesthetic introduced a darker Goth -influenced sensibility to the mainstream Emo scene. The 2000s subculture introduced the \"classic\" emo look, which was heavily influenced by Goth, Pop-Punk, and the \" Fashioncore \" trend within metalcore. This aesthetic prioritized darker colors, androgyny, and body modification."
  },
